Core Instrumentation

*   Clockwork Escapement Shakers: Handheld brass cylinders packed with crushed nickel-iron chondrites and watch pinions, agitated by miniature internal clock escapements.
*   The Meteor-Lithophone: Tuned bars sliced from deep-space meteors, struck with padded brass mallets to produce glass-like, unearthly bells that double as uplifting trance lead melodies.
*   1958 Gibson Les Paul & Ribbon Mic Array: Clean, tremolo-soaked rockabilly and jazz chord swells submerged in magnetic tape flutter.
*   Thermionic Vacuum-Tube Synthesizers: Primitive oscillators routed through vintage broadcast compressors to generate thick, buzzing basslines and soaring pad clouds.
*   Tape-Spliced Drum Kits: Hand-chopped magnetic tapes of 1950s swing drummers played at double speed to recreate classic jungle breaks with historical warmth.

